WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.103
-The nationwide protests
over George Floyd's murder

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:05.338
have been incredibly successful
in swaying public opinion.

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:07.740
And now even military leaders
are speaking out

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.976
against the president's
attempts to suppress them.

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:12.678
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:12.678 --> 00:00:16.482
♪♪

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:19.018
The country has been convulsing
with outrage over the brutal

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:22.054
murder of George Floyd at the
hands of Minneapolis police,

00:00:22.054 --> 00:00:24.990
and the president has decided
to respond with chilling

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:27.560
authoritarian threats
to unleash the military

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.695
on American citizens
in American cities,

00:00:29.695 --> 00:00:32.198
a threat he repeated yesterday
in an interview

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:35.234
with his former press secretary,
Sean Spicer.

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:37.137
-Will you send in the military

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:39.605
to any cities in particular to
restore that law and order?

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:41.708
-Well, it depends.
I don't think we'll have to.

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:44.744
We have very strong powers
to do it.

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:47.079
The National Guard is --
is customary,

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:49.949
and we have a very powerful
National Guard,

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:52.986
over 300,000 men and women.

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:55.021
And we can do pretty much
whatever we want.

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:56.656
-First of all, no, you can't.

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:59.225
Second, it's nice to see
Sean Spicer

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:02.228
somewhere other than the
bargain bin at Barnes &amp; Noble's.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:04.397
Sorry, holding up
the wobbly leg

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.665
on the bargain bin
at Barnes &amp; Noble's.

00:01:06.665 --> 00:01:09.135
I guess this is what's left
for you after you flunk out

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:10.470
from "Dancing with the Stars."

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.837
I'd hate to be this guy's agent.

00:01:11.837 --> 00:01:14.707
"Well, I never got a call back
from 'Naked and Afraid,'

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:17.009
but how would you like
to interview

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:18.778
the guy who fired you?

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.613
All right, pays scale."

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:22.048
It's clear the mass
demonstrations,

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:23.849
which have been
overwhelmingly peaceful,

00:01:23.849 --> 00:01:25.184
are having a major impact.

00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:27.853
Just last night, Trump's former
defense secretary,

00:01:27.853 --> 00:01:30.723
General James Mattis, expressed
support for the protests

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:33.292
and denounced Trump's
use of military police

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:35.862
to patrol D.C.
and tear-gas protesters

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:37.696
for his church photo op,
which of course,

00:01:37.696 --> 00:01:41.066
led Trump to lash out
with a bunch of cuckoo tweets.

00:01:41.066 --> 00:01:43.569
-"When I joined the military
some 50 years ago,

00:01:43.569 --> 00:01:47.139
I swore an oath to support
and defend the Constitution.

00:01:47.139 --> 00:01:50.376
Never did I dream that troops
taking that same oath

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.879
would be ordered under
any circumstance

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.613
to violate
the Constitutional rights

00:01:54.613 --> 00:01:56.048
of their fellow citizens."

00:01:56.048 --> 00:01:58.718
We must reject
and hold accountable

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:01.454
those in office who would
make a mockery

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.323
of our Constitution.

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:04.824
-Last night the president
tweeted,

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:08.394
"Probably the only thing
Barack Obama and I

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:11.130
have in common is that
we both have the honor

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:15.501
of firing Jim Mattis, the
world's most overrated general.

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:17.136
I asked for his
letter of resignation

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:18.838
and felt great about it.

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:22.208
His nickname was 'Chaos,'
which I didn't like,

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:24.444
and changed to 'Mad Dog.'"

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:26.078
-Okay, first of all,
he resigned.

00:02:26.078 --> 00:02:27.346
You didn't fire him.

00:02:27.346 --> 00:02:29.782
Second, you didn't come up
with the name "Mad Dog."

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:32.118
He's had it since at least 2004.

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:33.753
And we know you
didn't come up with it

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:37.122
because it's a cool nickname,
and your nicknames suck.

00:02:37.122 --> 00:02:38.724
Sorry.
Sorry, dude.

00:02:38.724 --> 00:02:40.560
If you'd come up with a nickname
for him, it would have been

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.895
something like "Lame James"
or "Jumpin' Jim."

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:44.630
[ As Trump ] "Jumpin' --
Jumpin' Jim Mattis.

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:46.899
You want to jump on up
to the microphone?

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:49.134
Always jumpin'.
Jumpin' Jim."

00:02:49.134 --> 00:02:51.604
Mattis' decision to speak out
is yet another indication

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:53.573
of the truly precarious moment
we're in.

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:55.474
Trump and the police
establishment are obviously

00:02:55.474 --> 00:02:58.243
threatened by the widespread
popularity of the protests,

00:02:58.243 --> 00:03:00.847
which have been both effective
and everywhere.

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:03.249
-Protests continue
nationwide today,

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:06.452
pleading for drastic changes
in America's law enforcement.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.087
[ Gunshot ]
Over the weekend,

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:10.723
demonstrations were reported
in all 50 states

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:12.425
and the District of Columbia.

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:15.428
-The map is finally all red, but
not for the reason Trump wants.

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:17.062
His aides probably
had to mute the TV

00:03:17.062 --> 00:03:18.564
to keep him from losing
his mind.

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:19.999
"Look, Mr. President,
the election's over

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:21.134
and you won all 50 states.

00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:22.668
Now you can go back
into the bunker

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:24.570
and stay there for
the next four years."

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:27.840
"Okay, but if anyone asks,
I'm not hiding in the bunker.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.476
I'm just checking to make sure
the light switches work, okay?

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:31.911
That's all."

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:34.980
And the demonstrations have
already clearly had results,

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:37.116
specifically in swaying
public opinion.

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:40.552
They're proving that direct mass
action in the streets works.

00:03:40.552 --> 00:03:42.788
One poll found that a majority
of the American public

00:03:42.788 --> 00:03:44.723
says that the anger
that led to these protests

00:03:44.723 --> 00:03:46.325
is fully justified.

00:03:46.325 --> 00:03:49.128
And another poll found
that 64% of American adults

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:51.430
were sympathetic to people
who are out protesting

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:52.765
right now.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:54.500
A little more than half
of rural residents said

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.135
they were sympathetic
to the protesters,

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:58.438
while seven out of ten
suburbanites agreed.

00:03:58.438 --> 00:04:00.939
Damn, usually the only thing you
can get that many suburbanites

00:04:00.939 --> 00:04:03.209
to agree on is their favorite
shopping mall food chain.

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:06.079
It's always Auntie Anne's.
And if you say Sbarro, you know,

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:07.680
just like a long look
in the mirror.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.182
If you're missing
Sbarro right now,

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:11.184
just take some Styrofoam
and melt some string cheese

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:12.785
on top of it.
There, boom.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:15.688
There's your Sbarro's.
Sbarro's!

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:18.057
That said, I would give anything
right now to go to a mall,

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:20.059
eat some Sbarro's and browse
one of those random kiosks

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:21.961
that sell calendars
with puppies on them.

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.662
Oh! You guys,
I miss going outside.

00:04:23.662 --> 00:04:26.732
And even when it's just to,
like, go right back inside.

00:04:26.732 --> 00:04:28.567
The point is, the protests have

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:30.436
profoundly swayed
public opinion.

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:33.772
And this kind of massive,
sustained political mobilization

00:04:33.772 --> 00:04:36.909
represents a direct threat
to the unjust system

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:39.078
of predatory policing
we currently have,

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:42.381
which is why the people who
benefit from that system

00:04:42.381 --> 00:04:45.485
are lashing out so aggressively,
one after another.

00:04:45.485 --> 00:04:47.887
We've watched countless videos
of local police departments

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:50.689
arresting or violently attacking
peaceful protesters,

00:04:50.689 --> 00:04:52.324
and reporters
lawfully exercising

00:04:52.324 --> 00:04:53.960
their First Amendment rights.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.662
In Ft. Lauderdale, for example,
an officer was caught on camera

00:04:56.662 --> 00:04:59.065
shoving a protester to
the ground who was peacefully

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:00.733
kneeling with her hands up.

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:03.269
And now "The Miami Herald"
reports that that officer

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:06.672
has been reviewed by
Internal Affairs for using force

00:05:06.672 --> 00:05:11.043
79 times in his roughly
3 1/2 years on the force.

00:05:11.043 --> 00:05:13.246
79 times in 3 1/2 years.

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:15.948
I haven't used shampoo that much
in the same time period.

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:17.383
And, granted,
I probably should have.

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:19.418
But how many times do you have
to get in trouble

00:05:19.418 --> 00:05:20.719
before you get fired?

00:05:20.719 --> 00:05:22.221
No other job works like that.

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:24.557
If a commercial airline pilot
had been investigated 79 times

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:26.625
for flying upside down
and doing barrel rolls

00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:28.327
while hammered on Goldschlager,

00:05:28.327 --> 00:05:30.630
we wouldn't be like,
"All right, man.

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.398
80 strikes, and you're out."

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:34.900
Of course, if it's more than
three strikes --

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:37.303
if it's ever more
than three strikes,

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:38.971
it's just
not strikes anymore.

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:40.372
It's tee-ball rules.

00:05:40.372 --> 00:05:41.840
No one's getting sent back
to the dugout.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:44.443
They just get sent off
to first base thinking,

00:05:44.443 --> 00:05:46.479
"I'm pretty good at baseball."

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:48.981
And then there's New York City,
where there have been countless

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:51.584
videos of police violently
escalating encounters

00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:55.687
with peaceful protesters and
inflicting abuse with impunity.

00:05:55.687 --> 00:05:58.290
On Tuesday, the NYPD trapped
thousands of protesters

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:00.325
in a dangerous situation
on the Manhattan Bridge

00:06:00.325 --> 00:06:02.428
for hours before letting them
enter Brooklyn.

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:04.764
-In New York City, thousands
of protesters,

00:06:04.764 --> 00:06:07.867
trapped on the Manhattan Bridge
for hours,

00:06:07.867 --> 00:06:10.335
police using barricades to
prevent them from leaving

00:06:10.335 --> 00:06:11.871
either side of the bridge,

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:15.274
a controversial tactic
known as "kettling."

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:17.943
-All right, first of all,
nothing that dangerous

00:06:17.943 --> 00:06:19.578
should have an adorable name
like "kettling."

00:06:19.578 --> 00:06:21.848
"Kettling" sounds like something
Ms. Doubtfire would make up

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:24.584
on the spot to trick the kids
into thinking she's British.

00:06:24.584 --> 00:06:26.385
"What are you doing,
Ms. Doubtfire?"

00:06:26.385 --> 00:06:28.721
[ As Mrs. Doubtfire ]
"Oh, just some 'kettling.'

00:06:28.721 --> 00:06:31.556
Oh, a bit -- a bit of the old
'kettling.'"

00:06:31.556 --> 00:06:34.093
And, yeah, I have run out

00:06:34.093 --> 00:06:35.928
of modern television shows
to watch,

00:06:35.928 --> 00:06:38.330
so I've been watching
old movies that seemed

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:40.899
normal at the time, but in
retrospect are kind of insane.

00:06:40.899 --> 00:06:43.302
Your husband puts on a wig,
and you don't recognize him?

00:06:43.302 --> 00:06:45.804
Okay! All right!

00:06:45.804 --> 00:06:48.474
Anyway, where was I?
Oh, right.

00:06:48.474 --> 00:06:50.376
Second, why the hell
are you trapping people

00:06:50.376 --> 00:06:51.711
on the Manhattan Bridge?

00:06:51.711 --> 00:06:53.346
Are you cops
or the Green Goblin?

00:06:53.346 --> 00:06:56.949
Again, Green Goblin, madman,
access to high-tech weaponry.

00:06:56.949 --> 00:07:00.486
You can't kill a teenager
in a unitard? Okay.

00:07:00.486 --> 00:07:02.121
Okay.

00:07:02.121 --> 00:07:03.922
The only time anyone should be
trapped for hours

00:07:03.922 --> 00:07:06.525
on the Manhattan Bridge is when
they decide to take a cab home

00:07:06.525 --> 00:07:08.060
during rush hour.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:10.495
And when that happens, you're
technically not trapped there,

00:07:10.495 --> 00:07:12.031
you live there.

00:07:12.031 --> 00:07:14.400
The last time I took a cab
across the Manhattan Bridge,

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:18.004
I was stuck so long, I started
getting mail there.

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:20.706
[ Taps ]

00:07:20.706 --> 00:07:23.509
Good rimshot, buddy.
Thank you.

00:07:23.509 --> 00:07:25.577
The scenes we've all watched
of police violently attacking

00:07:25.577 --> 00:07:27.880
protesters are more typical of
authoritarian regimes

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:29.681
than liberal democracies,
And of course,

00:07:29.681 --> 00:07:32.284
some of the most harrowing
examples have come from D.C.,

00:07:32.284 --> 00:07:34.019
where we've seen
military helicopters

00:07:34.019 --> 00:07:36.589
descend on protests
to scare them away,

00:07:36.589 --> 00:07:38.657
armed guards blocking the
Lincoln Memorial,

00:07:38.657 --> 00:07:41.227
caravans of military vehicles
rolling down streets,

00:07:41.227 --> 00:07:43.462
DEA agents authorized
to conduct

00:07:43.462 --> 00:07:45.264
covert surveillance
on protesters,

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:47.166
and unidentified
law enforcement officers

00:07:47.166 --> 00:07:50.969
without insignia or name badges
refusing to identify themselves.

00:07:50.969 --> 00:07:53.539
-Today we're about 60,
maybe 70 yards further away

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:55.341
from the White House
than we were yesterday,

00:07:55.341 --> 00:07:56.709
pushed back from that fence.

00:07:56.709 --> 00:07:58.043
And part of the story
here today is

00:07:58.043 --> 00:07:59.712
the increasing militarization

00:07:59.712 --> 00:08:02.949
and federalization
of the protest response

00:08:02.949 --> 00:08:05.484
on Washington, D.C.'s
city streets.

00:08:05.484 --> 00:08:07.720
These men behind me are with
the D.C. National Guard.

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:09.455
They were brought out here
a little bit earlier.

00:08:09.455 --> 00:08:12.525
They relieved a group
who wore no insignia,

00:08:12.525 --> 00:08:14.259
just federal law enforcement
officers

00:08:14.259 --> 00:08:15.628
who wouldn't identify
themselves,

00:08:15.628 --> 00:08:17.229
wouldn't tell me where
they were from,

00:08:17.229 --> 00:08:19.098
what agency they represented.

00:08:19.098 --> 00:08:21.333
-The worst part of this
is that every stoner

00:08:21.333 --> 00:08:24.303
who cornered me at a party
in college was right.

00:08:24.303 --> 00:08:26.772
We are living
in a police state.

00:08:26.772 --> 00:08:30.276
So, retroactive apologies,
Scooch.

00:08:30.276 --> 00:08:32.411
And of course the most
shocking example in D.C.

00:08:32.411 --> 00:08:34.613
was the violent attack
on peaceful protesters

00:08:34.613 --> 00:08:37.249
near the White House to make way
for the president to participate

00:08:37.249 --> 00:08:39.552
in his dumb photo op where
he walked over to a church

00:08:39.552 --> 00:08:41.354
and held up a Bible
that wasn't his

00:08:41.354 --> 00:08:42.955
like a teacher who just found
a porno mag

00:08:42.955 --> 00:08:44.590
in the back of a classroom.

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:47.893
"Guys, who is this?
Fess up or I'll have no choice

00:08:47.893 --> 00:08:50.862
but to conduct an investigation
and inspect it myself.

00:08:50.862 --> 00:08:53.465
You're better than this, guys.
You're better than this."

00:08:53.465 --> 00:08:55.934
Attacking peaceful protesters
exercising

00:08:55.934 --> 00:08:57.670
their Constitutional rights
just so the president

00:08:57.670 --> 00:09:00.105
can have a photo op
is a heinous crime

00:09:00.105 --> 00:09:01.607
against the Constitution.

00:09:01.607 --> 00:09:03.843
And as with all
authoritarian regimes,

00:09:03.843 --> 00:09:05.144
they can only
get away with it

00:09:05.144 --> 00:09:07.112
by warping reality
and lying about it.

00:09:07.112 --> 00:09:08.747
Yesterday, the White House
tried to claim

00:09:08.747 --> 00:09:10.582
they hadn't actually
used tear gas,

00:09:10.582 --> 00:09:13.785
but other chemicals that just
happened to cause tears.

00:09:13.785 --> 00:09:15.921
-No tear gas was used, and no
rubber bullets were used.

00:09:15.921 --> 00:09:18.157
-Chemical agents were used.
-So, again,

00:09:18.157 --> 00:09:20.425
no tear gas was used,
no rubber bullets were used.

00:09:20.425 --> 00:09:21.861
-Why are you making
that distinction?

00:09:21.861 --> 00:09:23.896
Chemical agents were used.
-Let me back up and --

00:09:23.896 --> 00:09:26.499
-We talked to an Episcopal
priest who said she was gassed.

00:09:26.499 --> 00:09:28.801
Others say they were tear-gassed
in that area.

00:09:28.801 --> 00:09:30.302
-Well, no one was tear-gassed.

00:09:30.302 --> 00:09:31.870
-Officials from the
administration claimed

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:34.073
that they did not use tear gas.

00:09:34.073 --> 00:09:36.675
All right, well, they used
pepper balls

00:09:36.675 --> 00:09:41.313
and smoke flashbangs,
which caused these images

00:09:41.313 --> 00:09:42.748
that you're seeing
right now.

00:09:42.748 --> 00:09:45.250
So, all right, if you want to
split hairs there.

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:48.420
It's a distinction without
a difference, right?

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:52.591
Pepper balls and flashbangs
share many similar effects

00:09:52.591 --> 00:09:58.196
of tear gas, including excessive
tearing, lachrymation,

00:09:58.196 --> 00:10:00.899
which CNN's team on the ground
witnessed.

00:10:00.899 --> 00:10:02.368
They experienced this.

00:10:02.368 --> 00:10:05.537
You can see the folks here in
front of you experiencing it.

00:10:05.537 --> 00:10:09.374
The president wants a correction
from the media that tear gas

00:10:09.374 --> 00:10:13.446
was not used, but in fact
by his own CDC's classification,

00:10:13.446 --> 00:10:15.080
it was tear gas.

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:16.615
-If the CDC says it's tear gas,

00:10:16.615 --> 00:10:18.250
he's definitely not
going to listen to them.

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:20.652
The CDC also says sticking
Tide to-go pens up your nose

00:10:20.652 --> 00:10:22.721
won't cure coronavirus,
but I'm almost certain

00:10:22.721 --> 00:10:24.289
Trump's at least tried it.

00:10:24.289 --> 00:10:27.492
"I can tell it's working because
my brain is on fire."

00:10:27.492 --> 00:10:29.695
But the lies are not working,
and you can tell because

00:10:29.695 --> 00:10:31.763
even Trump's Defense Secretary
Mark Esper

00:10:31.763 --> 00:10:34.065
is now distancing himself
from the photo op,

00:10:34.065 --> 00:10:35.534
although he's doing it

00:10:35.534 --> 00:10:37.903
with one of the most
laughable excuses imaginable.

00:10:37.903 --> 00:10:40.205
Esper, who accompanied Trump
to the church

00:10:40.205 --> 00:10:42.207
after the protesters
had been attacked,

00:10:42.207 --> 00:10:44.977
told NBC News, "I didn't know
where I was going."

00:10:44.977 --> 00:10:46.979
Esper said, he believed
they were going to observe

00:10:46.979 --> 00:10:49.581
the vandalized bathroom
in Lafayette Square.

00:10:49.581 --> 00:10:52.952
Well, in his defense, anytime
you follow Trump anywhere,

00:10:52.952 --> 00:10:57.089
you probably expect to see
a bathroom get destroyed.

00:10:58.791 --> 00:11:01.460
[ Taps ]
Oh, even better!

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:03.762
You're getting
really good at it.

00:11:03.762 --> 00:11:06.065
All right, just don't overstay
your welcome.

00:11:06.065 --> 00:11:07.532
Seriously, you thought
you were going to go see

00:11:07.532 --> 00:11:08.701
a vandalized bathroom?

00:11:08.701 --> 00:11:10.936
You don't need
to gas protesters for that.

00:11:10.936 --> 00:11:12.972
Just go to any rest stop
on I-95.

00:11:12.972 --> 00:11:15.574
In fairness to Esper,
I can definitely see Trump

00:11:15.574 --> 00:11:18.176
wanting to take a field trip
to see a vandalized bathroom.

00:11:18.176 --> 00:11:20.012
"The wall said to call this
number for a good time.

00:11:20.012 --> 00:11:22.447
Should we? I mean it feels like
we're living in a bad time.

00:11:22.447 --> 00:11:24.149
Maybe a good time is exactly
what we need

00:11:24.149 --> 00:11:25.751
to turn this thing around.
Should we just call?

00:11:25.751 --> 00:11:26.952
Use the White House number.

00:11:26.952 --> 00:11:29.388
I don't want to use my cell
phone minutes."

00:11:29.388 --> 00:11:31.389
This is what authoritarian
regimes do.

00:11:31.389 --> 00:11:33.925
They defend violent crackdowns
on peaceful protesters

00:11:33.925 --> 00:11:35.827
by spreading lies
and disinformation.

00:11:35.827 --> 00:11:38.263
And yet the Republican Party
is in most cases

00:11:38.263 --> 00:11:40.966
either idly standing by
or openly embracing

00:11:40.966 --> 00:11:43.802
calls for military violence
towards American citizens.

00:11:43.802 --> 00:11:46.572
Arkansas Senator Tom Cotton
wrote a chilling op-ed

00:11:46.572 --> 00:11:48.908
for "The New York Times"
called "Send in the Troops,"

00:11:48.908 --> 00:11:51.176
in which he lied repeatedly
about the demonstrations

00:11:51.176 --> 00:11:53.078
and called on the president
to invoke a law known

00:11:53.078 --> 00:11:54.579
as the "Insurrection Act"

00:11:54.579 --> 00:11:56.514
to send the military
into American cities

00:11:56.514 --> 00:11:58.117
to put down the protests.

00:11:58.117 --> 00:11:59.751
Cotton wrote,
"One thing above all else

00:11:59.751 --> 00:12:01.887
will restore order to
our streets, an overwhelming

00:12:01.887 --> 00:12:03.589
show of force to disperse,

00:12:03.589 --> 00:12:06.325
detain, and ultimately
deter law breakers."

00:12:06.325 --> 00:12:07.960
Holy [bleep], dude.

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:10.462
Did you steal that line
from General Hux?

00:12:10.462 --> 00:12:12.798
These guys want to tear up
the Constitution so badly

00:12:12.798 --> 00:12:15.868
because they want to be ruled
by a dictator so badly.

00:12:15.868 --> 00:12:17.970
Nothing would make them happier
than to throw a party

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:20.472
celebrating the end of democracy
and load a confetti cannon

00:12:20.472 --> 00:12:22.241
with scraps
from the Bill of Rights.

00:12:22.241 --> 00:12:25.210
But as sinister as this op-ed
is, the more shocking thing

00:12:25.210 --> 00:12:27.179
is that the "Times" opinion page
chose to run it.

00:12:27.179 --> 00:12:30.082
I mean, what are you guys doing?
Our democracy is on a precipice,

00:12:30.082 --> 00:12:31.950
and you decide
to give it a push?

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:34.720
I mean, just because
it's a terrible opinion

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:36.622
doesn't mean it deserves

00:12:36.622 --> 00:12:39.058
to be on the "New York Times"
op-ed page.

00:12:39.058 --> 00:12:41.527
I mean you wouldn't want to read
"Baby seals are asking for it,

00:12:41.527 --> 00:12:42.761
club away."

00:12:42.761 --> 00:12:44.663
A fun joke to tell
with no live audience.

00:12:44.663 --> 00:12:46.966
It definitely would have
groaned for it.

00:12:46.966 --> 00:12:49.902
And yet here, the same sound
all the time.

00:12:49.902 --> 00:12:52.337
The "Times'" editorial page
editor James Bennett

00:12:52.337 --> 00:12:54.873
responded to backlash
over the op-ed writing,

00:12:54.873 --> 00:12:57.242
"'Times' opinion owes it
to our readers to show them

00:12:57.242 --> 00:12:59.912
counterarguments, particularly
those made by people

00:12:59.912 --> 00:13:01.479
in a position to set policy.

00:13:01.479 --> 00:13:04.149
We understand that many readers
find Senator Cotton's argument

00:13:04.149 --> 00:13:05.450
painful, even dangerous.

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:07.185
We believe that is one reason

00:13:07.185 --> 00:13:09.354
it requires public scrutiny
and debate."

00:13:09.354 --> 00:13:11.656
Wait, so your argument is you
had to print a bad column

00:13:11.656 --> 00:13:13.525
in your newspaper so everyone
would know it's bad?

00:13:13.525 --> 00:13:14.826
I mean, that logic
makes no sense.

00:13:14.826 --> 00:13:16.395
If you go to a five-star
restaurant, the chef

00:13:16.395 --> 00:13:19.031
doesn't serve you Arby's first
just to make sure

00:13:19.031 --> 00:13:20.599
you know it tastes
like [bleep].

00:13:20.599 --> 00:13:22.501
You're not legally obligated
to run fascist calls

00:13:22.501 --> 00:13:24.569
for military occupation
in your newspaper.

00:13:24.569 --> 00:13:25.970
Tom Cotton is a senator.

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:27.640
He has plenty of ways to get
his opinions out there.

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:29.909
C-SPAN.
All right, that's a bad example.

00:13:29.909 --> 00:13:32.778
But if your policy is that
you're going to run bad columns

00:13:32.778 --> 00:13:35.246
full of lies for the sake of
hearing counterarguments,

00:13:35.246 --> 00:13:38.283
then I'm officially requesting
that you run my op-ed,

00:13:38.283 --> 00:13:40.886
"James Bennett's favorite movie
of all time is 'Cats.'"

00:13:40.886 --> 00:13:43.255
I dare you to print it.

00:13:43.255 --> 00:13:46.559
Or, are you too afraid of
my controversial opinions?

00:13:46.559 --> 00:13:48.727
The president and the police
establishment are lashing out

00:13:48.727 --> 00:13:51.296
at nationwide protests because
those protests threaten

00:13:51.296 --> 00:13:54.132
a racist, unjust system
that serves the powerful.

00:13:54.132 --> 00:13:57.036
They're deeply invested
in protecting that system

00:13:57.036 --> 00:13:59.471
because at the core of it
is the belief

00:13:59.471 --> 00:14:00.839
that the people in charge...

00:14:00.839 --> 00:14:02.741
-Can do pretty much
whatever we want.

00:14:02.741 --> 00:14:04.409
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:14:04.409 --> 00:14:07.746
♪♪

